WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.344
Frame a comparison.

00:00:01.344 --> 00:00:06.272
A chart begins with a decision the reader needs to make.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:10.752
Connect the question, measure, and comparison before choosing a chart.

00:00:10.752 --> 00:00:13.439
Ask which lesson format retains learners.

00:00:13.439 --> 00:00:16.575
Define completion as a share of starts.

00:00:16.575 --> 00:00:19.711
Compare formats over the same time window.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.551
Choose a clear visual encoding.

00:00:22.551 --> 00:00:27.152
Select a chart that matches the relationship in your data.

00:00:27.152 --> 00:00:31.293
Use common scales where readers need to compare quantities.

00:00:31.293 --> 00:00:34.054
Compare category totals with aligned bars.

00:00:34.054 --> 00:00:37.735
Use a line for change across regular dates.

00:00:37.735 --> 00:00:40.496
Plot paired numeric values as points.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.410
Annotate the finding.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:46.640
An annotation connects a visible pattern to its context.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.870
Make the observation precise and distinguish evidence from interpretation.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:54.160
Point to the exact date or category.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.451
State the size of the observed change.

00:00:57.451 --> 00:01:00.741
Explain a known event or data limitation.

